# OpenArch workspace: {{ .Config.Name }}

This folder was created by `openarch init`. `openarch.yaml` is the source of truth.
To change the deployment, edit `openarch.yaml` and run `openarch render`.

## Endpoints

| Service | URL |
| --- | --- |
| OpenArch API | {{ .Config.URL }} |
| Swagger UI | {{ .Config.URL }}/swagger-ui/index.html |
| Health | {{ .Config.URL }}/actuator/health |
{{- if .Config.Has "dashboards" }}
| OpenSearch Dashboards | http://{{ .HostIP }}:5601 |
{{- end }}
{{- if .Config.Has "opensearch" }}
| OpenSearch | http://{{ .HostIP }}:9200 |
{{- end }}
{{- if .Config.Has "mongodb" }}
| MongoDB | mongodb://{{ .HostIP }}:27017/?directConnection=true |
{{- end }}
{{- if .Config.Has "debug" }}
| Java debug (JDWP) | {{ .HostIP }}:5005 |
{{- end }}

## Credentials

The admin user and password are in `.env.local`. Keep that file private.
`config/users.yml` holds only a bcrypt hash of the password. OpenArch reads it at startup.
{{- if eq .Config.TLS.Mode "self-signed" }}

## TLS

The certificate in `certs/` is self-signed, so browsers and clients do not trust it by default.
It is valid for {{ .Config.ServerName }}, localhost and 127.0.0.1.
{{- else if eq .Config.TLS.Mode "custom" }}

## TLS

The proxy uses the certificate `{{ .Config.TLS.Cert }}` and the key `{{ .Config.TLS.Key }}`.
{{- end }}

## Storage

{{ if .Volume -}}
Data is kept in Docker named volumes: `{{ .Config.Name }}_mongodb-data`, `{{ .Config.Name }}_opensearch-data` and `{{ .Config.Name }}_openarch-data`.
`docker compose down` keeps them. `docker compose down -v` deletes them.
{{- else if .Bind -}}
Data is kept in `{{ .DataDir }}`: one folder each for MongoDB, OpenSearch and OpenArch files.
{{- else -}}
Storage is `none`: no data is kept when the containers are removed.
{{- end }}

## Run without the CLI

```
docker compose up -d
docker compose ps
docker compose logs -f openarch-app
docker compose down
```
